    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` field as a derived, read-only attribute of an owner, following the existing pattern for other derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `customerCode`).\n\n**Two changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `membershipNumber` read-only property to the `Owner` schema (which drives DTO generation), documented as `'<customerCode>-M<YY>'`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` for `membershipNumber` backed by a new `membershipNumber(owner)` helper that formats `String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", customerCode, registrationDate.getYear() % 100)` \u2014 e.g. `SMI-0007` + year 2026 \u2192 `SMI-0007-M26`. It returns `null` when either `customerCode` or `registrationDate` is absent, which guards the seed owners (their `customer_code`/`registration_date` columns are null) against an NPE.\n\nNo OfficeFloor pipeline change was needed: membership number is purely derived from the owner's own persisted fields, so computing it at response-mapping time matches how `displayName`/`initials` already work, and it's automatically correct for both create-response and GET.\n\nThe `coreMembershipNumberFormat` acceptance test passes, and the full test suite builds green.",
